# An ALLOWLIST, for the same reason the sdist is one (pyproject.toml, [tool.hatch.build.targets.sdist]):
# a denylist needs a new line for every new scratch directory and fails by shipping it, an allowlist fails
# by a missing file, which is loud. A checkout holds a developer's own config/prometheus.yaml, env files and
# .claude/worktrees; none of it can reach the build context, so none of it can reach a layer.
#
# Everything the Dockerfile COPYs is listed here (tests/test_docker_image.py checks both directions).
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!src/
!templates/
!config/prometheus.yaml.default
!config/model_registry.yaml
!packaging/macos/release-tools.txt
!packaging/macos/build-constraints.txt

# Never, even inside an allowed directory.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
